  "display_pins": {
    "sck": 18,
    "mosi": 23,
    "cs": 15,
    "dc": 2,
    "reset": 4,
    "backlight": -1
  },
  "verified": false,
  "notes": "Classic ESP32 (no GDMA): rows go out through LovyanGFX's DMA, one at a time. SCK 18 and MOSI 23 are VSPI's own pins. GPIO16 and GPIO17 are taken by the PSRAM on WROVER modules, GPIO34 to GPIO39 have no pull-ups. Revision 3 chips only (all WROVER-E modules), so the old PSRAM cache workaround is off."
}
